## 6. Scalability Improvements

> [!WARNING]
> The current architecture has several bottlenecks that will break at 500+ employees.

### Backend Architecture

| Issue | Current State | Recommendation |
|-------|---------------|----------------|
| **Monolithic Server** | `index.js` is 1,161 lines — all auth, middleware, routes | Split into proper MVC: controllers/, middlewares/, validators/ |
| **No Caching** | Every API call hits DB directly | Add Redis for session cache, attendance summaries, dashboard KPIs |
| **No Connection Pooling** | SQLite has single-writer lock | Move to PostgreSQL with connection pool (already supported but not default) |
| **No Queue System** | Payroll generation is synchronous | Use BullMQ / Agenda for payroll processing, report generation |
| **No Rate Limiting Per Route** | Only login has rate limiting | Add per-route rate limiting for all write operations |
| **Worker Threads** | `workers/` directory exists but minimal usage | Offload heavy operations (bulk import, payroll calc) to worker threads |

### Frontend Architecture

| Issue | Recommendation |
|-------|----------------|
| Loads ALL data on login (employees, attendance, payroll, leaves, expenses) | Implement lazy loading — fetch data per page/module |
| `Dashboard.tsx` is 61,744 bytes (huge!) | Split into sub-components: KPI cards, charts, activity feed |
| `CameraPunchWidget.tsx` is 78,173 bytes | Extract face recognition, camera, UI into separate modules |
| No code splitting | Add `React.lazy()` for route-level code splitting |
| 30-second global auto-sync | Replace with WebSocket/SSE for real-time updates |

